#{ ===========================================================================
   HAVING AND KNOWING AT THE PANEL -- direction and relation, said apart.

   The flat panel (12.2) says WHERE with its sections and WHAT with its
   markers -- two questions, two words, never one word answering both:

     in: / out:   DIRECTION. An in: entry arrives with the call; an out:
                  entry leaves at give. That is all the section says.
     (unmarked)   HAVING -- the ground state. An unmarked in: entry is
                  CUSTODY IN: the giver's name dies, this work now HAS --
                  and owes the end of what it has (give onward or
                  destruct, 0.3). An unmarked out: entry is CUSTODY OUT:
                  at give it; moves WHOLE to the caller, who has it now.
     known:       ACQUAINTANCE. The entry is a VIEW: the work may read
                  what it is told; it takes no responsibility and confers
                  none. A known may be Nothing -- so every OPERATION on
                  it demands a dominating gate (0.5, SEMANTICS 28); where
                  the flow makes Nothing impossible, the access is fine.
     had:         the optional VISIBILITY marker -- having spelled out
                  loud; it adds nothing the ground state does not say.

   Giving is moving, never copying: one object, one debt, one haver at a
   time -- and THE GIVE LEAVES NOTHING BEHIND: the giver holds Nothing in
   the given thing's place; access to the given is impossible
   (HAVE_KNOW_BE (2)). The trace of responsibility is the chain of
   havings; the knowns stand beside it, reading.

   HONESTY NOTE: the call-site 'give' marker and the ledger that PROVES
   the chain bind the future type document (SEMANTICS 23, deferred); the
   for:-from: loop already spells its two custody flavours (13.5).
   =========================================================================== }

score : class {
    points: float;
    from : work
}

+score.from : work(in: start                #{ a value, had by copy }
                   out: s : score           #{ custody OUT: the caller will HAVE }
                   signals: negative) {
    if: start < 0 { signal negative; }
    s = start;
    give s;                    # the out-bundle leaves HERE, named
}

#{ A disposal work is the mirror: custody IN, and the debt ends inside. }

-score : work(in: s : score) {              #{ unmarked: the debt arrives }
    give;
}

#{ known: is the VIEW -- and the view may be Nothing, so the body GATES
   before it operates: the gate narrows, the operation stands on narrowed
   ground. No gate, no operation -- the checker holds the law. }

bonus : work(in: known: base, factor
             out: total
             signals: unknown) {
    if: base == Nothing { signal unknown; }
    total = base * factor;
    give total;
}

Demo : reactor(in: cmd) {
    s: float; t: float;
  show : behavior {
    SHOW => {
        .s = score.from(start = 40) else: { negative => ; }
        .t = bonus(.s, 2) else: { unknown => ; }
    }
}
}

#{ The demonstration runs as a small PLANT (pipe ruling): a script feeder
   wired to the Demo reactor; the harness replays SHOW. }

plant : work() {
    f = script("SHOW");
    d = Demo();
    f ----> d;
    give;
}
